Description: Errors for four inputs the zfs writer can't write
 A hard link whose names are in two datasets was written as a directory
 entry that held the other dataset's object number, which corrupted the
 pool. A symbolic link target too long for the bonus buffer, and two
 datasets with one mount point, failed assertions. A tree with no dataset
 mounted at the root path dereferenced a null pointer. All four are now
 errors that name the cause.
Author: The Blueberry Pie OS Authors
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-15

